Allow Manifest V2 extensions again (full uBlock Origin).

M151 still ships the whole MV2 runtime: MV2 manifests parse, webRequestBlocking and persistent background pages are
there. The only gate is ShouldDisableLegacyExtensions() in manifest_v2_handler.cc, which returns true outside tests.
Its three callers (install check, enable check, disabling already installed MV2 extensions at startup) all go through
it, so returning false restores MV2 everywhere. Unpacked MV2 extensions still get a deprecation warning.

diff -ru a/src/extensions/browser/manifest_v2_handler.cc b/src/extensions/browser/manifest_v2_handler.cc
--- a/src/extensions/browser/manifest_v2_handler.cc	2026-11-18 08:00:00
+++ b/src/extensions/browser/manifest_v2_handler.cc	2026-11-18 08:00:00
@@ -109,10 +109,6 @@
 // Returns true if legacy extensions should be disabled.
 bool ShouldDisableLegacyExtensions() {
-  if (g_allow_mv2_for_testing) {
-    // We allow legacy MV2 extensions for testing purposes.
-    return false;
-  }
-
-  return true;
+  // Our build keeps MV2 (0104-allow-mv2-extensions.patch).
+  return false;
 }

